Ported third-party code
-----------------------

`oh-package.json5` declares no runtime dependency: every layer the app needs was
ported into this repository rather than pulled in. Each port carries the
upstream class it was written from in its file header, so the derivation can be
checked file by file. What was ported, and under which license:

* NewPipeExtractor 0.26.5 — the extractor, every service and link handler.
  GNU General Public License, version 3.
  https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipeExtractor

* RxJava 3.1.12 and RxAndroid 3.0.2 — the reactive layer under
  `entry/src/main/ets/common/rx/`.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/ReactiveX/RxJava

* jsoup 1.22.2 — the HTML parser and selector engine under
  `entry/src/main/ets/common/extractor/html/`.
  MIT License.
  https://jsoup.org/

* Markwon 4.6.2 (core and linkify) — the description renderer under
  `entry/src/main/ets/common/text/`.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/noties/Markwon

* PrettyTime 5.0.8.Final — the relative-time formatter
  `entry/src/main/ets/common/i18n/PrettyTime.ts`.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/ocpsoft/prettytime

* NoNonsense-FilePicker — the in-app directory picker under
  `entry/src/main/ets/pages/CustomFilePickerFragmentPage.ets` and
  `entry/src/main/ets/common/file/FilePicker.ts`, which NewPipe vendors as a
  fork and which this port needs because folder selection is not available to a
  phone app on HarmonyOS.
  Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/spacecowboy/NoNonsense-FilePicker


Bundled upstream assets
-----------------------

* `entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/aboutlibraries.json` and
  `entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/licenses/*.txt` are carried over from
  upstream NewPipe and are what the in-app About screen shows. They describe the
  libraries of the ANDROID build; this port ships none of them as binaries.

* `entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/po_token.html` is upstream's
  `app/src/main/assets/po_token.html`, used by the YouTube extractor.

* The launcher icon, the splash artwork and the in-app vector icons under
  `entry/src/main/resources/base/media/` come from upstream NewPipe's own
  resources.

* The screenshots under `assets/screenshots/` were captured on the port itself.


Build and test tooling
----------------------

`@ohos/hypium` and `@ohos/hamock` are devDependencies only: they run the host
test suite and are not part of the installed HAP. Both are published by Huawei
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
